  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) ion-ion interaction energy is inversely proportional to the distance between ions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math><br />(ii) dipole-dipole interaction energy is inversely proportional to the third power of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced></math><br />(iii) The interaction energy of London force is inversely proportional to sixth power of distance between two interaction particles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced></math>"
